\description{
An example input dataframe structured for use with \code{\link{monteProd}}.
Examples exist for all possibilities of input data (radiolysis and/or serpentinization)
use of known rock properties (rock density and porosity) or literature values called from \code{\link{CRPPData}}.
Intended to demonstrate the breadth of inputs that are allowable for
hydrogen and helium production modelling.
}
\details{
Each row represents one sample. All continuous input parameters are
specified as truncated normal distributions defined by a minimum, maximum,
mean, and standard deviation. These bounds are passed to
\code{\link{rtrunc}} internally by \code{\link{monteProd}} to generate
Monte Carlo parameter distributions for each trial.

To run a radiolysis simulation with this dataset:
\preformatted{
data("structuredDF")
results <- monteProd(structuredDF, numGen = 50, rad = TRUE)
}
}
